  "scenario_narratives": {
    "base": "Handset components plateau (optics and casings under ASP/volume pressure) while acoustics/EM drives share gains, automotive acoustics (PSS) and the heat-dissipation ramp carry mid-single-digit group growth; margins hold near the FY2022-25 ~20% EBITDA band, capex stays disciplined at ~8.5% of revenue.",
    "bull": "AAC's materials/precision platform converts into the new tracks management sizes at RMB10bn-scale -- flagship VC and active cooling, data-centre liquid cooling, robotics actuators, AR waveguides, WLG for CPO -- so revenue compounds ~10% and mix pushes EBITDA margin toward 23%.",
    "bear": "Customer concentration bites: the largest customer re-sources or squeezes price as memory costs eat handset BOMs, optics keeps shrinking, auto price war compresses PSS margins, and the group is left a low-growth, capex-heavy supplier at ~16.5% EBITDA margin."
  },
  "valuation_philosophy": {
    "summary": "Mid-cycle owner-FCF valuation of a cyclical, customer-concentrated precision-components maker. Year-1 owner FCF is built from components at ~8% of revenue rather than FY2025's 14% reported margin, which included working-capital releases that cannot recur and follows years in which equipment deposits made FCF negative. Risk is charged in the flows and weights, once.",
    "key_risks_to_valuation": [
      "Customer concentration: loss of share at the largest smartphone customer",
      "Smartphone unit decline and memory-cost squeeze on handset BOMs (1H 2026 IDC -4.1%/-6.7%)",
