    "wacc_rationale": "Built in CNY/HKD terms: China 10y govt ~1.9%, plus a HK-listed China-manufacturing ERP of ~6.5% x beta ~1.15 = cost of equity ~9.4-9.9%; debt is cheap (bank loans 2.1-4.2%, notes) but small at ~6% net gearing, so WACC 9.5% is essentially the cost of equity. Single WACC across scenarios: smartphone cyclicality and Apple concentration are priced in the scenario flows and weights, not stacked as a premium (adaptation f).",
