    "notes": "Model: owner-FCF DCF (component route) with non-US/cyclical adaptations. AAC is an operating precision-components manufacturer (acoustics and electromagnetic drives, optics, precision mechanics and heat dissipation, automotive acoustics via PSS, sensors/semis) -- routing row 'operating company, non-US or cyclical'. First valuation of this ticker; no prior DCF or memory entry. Normalisation: reported FCF is lumpy -- FY2020-21 were negative on RMB2.2bn of equipment deposits inside capex, and FY2023-25 were flattered by RMB0.6-0.9bn/yr working-capital releases (cash conversion cycle cut to <20 days). The forward build therefore uses mid-cycle components (capex 8.4-8.8% of revenue vs 7.5-8.4% FY2023-25 and 14-23% FY2017-21; working capital consuming 8% of each revenue increment) rather than FY2025's 14% FCF margin; year-1 owner-FCF margin ~8%, against a FY2017-25 cumulative reported FCF margin of 7.9%. Interest income (RMB193m) not stripped: the group is net debt, not net cash. Bridge timing: FY0 revenue is FY2025 while debt/cash/shares are 30 Jun 2026 -- the 1H 2026 cash flow sits inside year 1 and the balance sheet, a small conservative overlap. Buybacks: active repurchaser (RMB955m FY2025), so the flat count is funded. SBC-zero market in practice: house and street differ by ~0.05% of revenue and the band is not meaningful.",
